{
 "_readme": [
  "THE QUERY VOCABULARY for importers/discover_facebook.py. Nan, 2026-09-06: 'I bet there's thousands of",
  "live, active records on FB for entities that WANT to be publicly shared, and don't exist online or on",
  "Open Street Map. All categories, no limits.'",
  "",
  "Two dimensions. WORDS: tier 1 is every shelf label in data/categories.json (the site's own tree); tier 2",
  "is the words businesses use for THEMSELVES — Facebook's page-category strings, Thai and English. The",
  "tier-2 seed below is hand-written; it GROWS in perpetuity, because facebook-reader harvests",
  "attrs.fbCategories off every page it reads and reconcile() folds new ones in here with their date and",
  "how often this city actually uses them. Mining our own record names was tried and rejected: 3,481 of",
  "19,462 Thai names begin โรงเรียน and 2,657 วัด, so the catalogue's names reproduce exactly the OSM bias",
  "this lane exists to correct.",
  "",
  "GEO: province first, then each อำเภอ — 25 in Chiang Mai, 18 in Chiang Rai. The amphoe pass is what makes",
  "the sweep cover the province rather than the city: a shop in สันกำแพง or แม่สาย is not returned by a",
  "search that says เชียงใหม่. It is ADAPTIVE — a word only earns its 43 amphoe queries once the province",
  "query for that word has returned at least one page, so dead words cost 1 query, not 44.",
  "",
  "Nothing here is a claim about the city. A word with no results means this search found none."
 ],
